{"title": "Snatcher", "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"druid-infobox druid-container noexcerpt\" id=\"druid-container-1\"><div><div class=\"druid-title\">Snatcher</div></div><div class=\"druid-section-container\"><div class=\"druid-main-image\"><div class=\"druid-main-images-labels druid-tabs\"><div class=\"druid-main-images-label druid-tab druid-toggleable druid-title-tab focused\" data-druid=\"1-1\" data-druid-tab-key=\"In-Game\">In-Game</div></div><a href=\"/wiki/File:Snatcher.jpg\" class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Snatcher.jpg\" src=\"/images/thumb/Snatcher.jpg/250px-Snatcher.jpg?4025ac\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"250\" height=\"141\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/Snatcher.jpg/375px-Snatcher.jpg?4025ac 1.5x, /images/thumb/Snatcher.jpg/500px-Snatcher.jpg?4025ac 2x\" data-file-width=\"1920\" data-file-height=\"1080\" /></a></div></div><div class=\"druid-section-container\"><div data-druid-section=\"Information\"><div class=\"druid-section druid-section-Information\">Information</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-VariantOf\" data-druid-section-row=\"Information\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-VariantOf\">Variant Of</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-VariantOf druid-data-nonempty\">\nThumper</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-InternalID\" data-druid-section-row=\"Information\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-InternalID\">Internal ID</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-InternalID druid-data-nonempty\">\nSnatcher</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-MaxCount\" data-druid-section-row=\"Information\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-MaxCount\">Max Count</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-MaxCount druid-data-nonempty\">\n4</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-PowerLevel\" data-druid-section-row=\"Information\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-PowerLevel\">Power Level</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-PowerLevel druid-data-nonempty\">\n3</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-CauseofDeath\" data-druid-section-row=\"Information\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-CauseofDeath\">Cause of Death</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-CauseofDeath druid-data-nonempty\">\nMauling</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-IsBodyRecoverable\" data-druid-section-row=\"Information\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-IsBodyRecoverable\">Is Body Recoverable?</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-IsBodyRecoverable druid-data-nonempty\">\nYes</div></div></div><div class=\"druid-section-container\"><div data-druid-section=\"Stats\"><div class=\"druid-section druid-section-Stats\">Stats</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-Health\" data-druid-section-row=\"Stats\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-Health\">Health</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-Health druid-data-nonempty\">\n8</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-Damage\" data-druid-section-row=\"Stats\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-Damage\">Damage</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-Damage druid-data-nonempty\">\n40</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-DoorSpeedMultiplier\" data-druid-section-row=\"Stats\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-DoorSpeedMultiplier\">Door Speed Multiplier</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-DoorSpeedMultiplier druid-data-nonempty\">\n0.3</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-StunTimeMultiplier\" data-druid-section-row=\"Stats\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-StunTimeMultiplier\">Stun Time Multiplier</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-StunTimeMultiplier druid-data-nonempty\">\n0.5</div></div></div></div>\n<p>The <b>Snatcher</b> is a hostile entity and variant of the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://lethal.miraheze.org/wiki/Thumper\">Thumper</a> added by <b>Wesley's Ememy Variants</b>. It has an oval-shaped body comprised of a muddy-like substance similar to the sludge it resides in. It has several limbs and hands, two glowing eyes, and a mouth constantly spitting sludge onto the floor.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Mechanics\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Mechanics\">&gt; Mechanics</span></h2>\n<p>Not to be confused with the several other encounters players can have with the <b>Snatcher</b> in the <a href=\"/wiki/Deep_Sewers\" title=\"Deep Sewers\"><b>Deep Sewers</b></a>, the actual entity behaves similarly to a Thumper. It will roam around the interior until spotting a player to chase, rapidly accelerating while moving and decelerating when having to turn or after hitting a wall. It will deal 40 damage to players that come into contact with its main body. Due to the hitbox of the <b>Snatcher</b> being larger and higher up than the Thumper, it is more feasible, albeit still ill-advised, to fight and kill it with a knife.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Spawn_Conditions\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Spawn_Conditions\">&gt; Spawn Conditions</span></h2>\n<p>The <b>Snatcher</b> has a 50% chance to spawn within the <a href=\"/wiki/Deep_Sewers\" title=\"Deep Sewers\"><b>Deep Sewers</b></a> at exactly 5pm. A roar can be heard at this time while in the interior as an indicator for it spawning. This spawn does not contribute to total Power Level, and the technical Max Count and Power Level of the <b>Snatcher</b> only matter if players modify spawn tables to spawn the <b>Snatcher</b> elsewhere.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Bestiary_Entry\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Bestiary_Entry\">&gt; Bestiary Entry</span></h2>\n<table class=\"article-table mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" data-expandtext=\"\u25bc\" data-collapsetext=\"\u25b2\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Snatcher <span style=\"padding-left:0.5em;\">&#x2060;</span>\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<table style=\"border: 15px solid #8E8E83; font-size: 135%; font-family: Tomorrow; color: #01A801; border-spacing: 0px;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"padding: 25px; background-color: #151515;\">SNATCHER<br /><br />Sigurd's danger level: 65%<br /><br />Scientific name: Mudcantis-suratin<br /><br />The Mudcantis-suratin or more commonly known as the Snatcher is a part of the Uranuh family. It is a muddy creature which prefers warm, swampy areas where it is most commonly found. Female Snatchers tend to have a soft, muddy skin covered in tiny tendrils which are often mistaken for thick hairs. Male snatchers have a thick, hard calcium plate below their \u201cface\u201d under a thinner, rubbery layer of skin.<br /><br />Snatchers have a great amount of appendages, growing more as they get older, ending in hand-like shapes. While they look like hands they only resemble them and do not contain any Intrinsic muscles. However these are very strong and are their main form of travel both underwater and on land.<br /><br />Snatchers are not naturally aggressive creatures despite their intimidating look. They prefer to stick to the shadows or cloudy lakes and watch from a distance. The females are entirely herbivores while the males do snatch, drown and digest small creatures entirely for the calcium required to grow their face plate.<br /><br />However it is not always safe to assume a snatcher won\u2019t harm you. It will act in self defense if it feels threatened with measures ranging from spitting thick sludge at you to violently swinging its appendages at you.<br />This act of defense is also amplified, specifically in females if anyone or anything approaches their nesting area. Chasing down and often viciously killing those who get too close to her young.<br /><br />The mating process of snatchers is often fatal for the male as it requires them to briefly suffocate within the female. On the occasion of death, the female will mourn the male in their own unique way. The male\u2019s skin gets repurposed to create a softer bed for the eggs once they are eventually laid. While the face plate will be hidden somewhere deep underwater as a form of burial. They often visit the burial site and seek to protect it from any intruders.<br /><br />While on the surface Snatchers are often described as monsters due to their name and look, they are very emotional and have a surprisingly good memory. There have been several counts of people befriending a Snatcher with them still remembering that person a decade later.<br /><br />It is recommended to stay away from their nests and leave them be when encountered in the wild. While deaths by snatchers are not common, it is a possibility.\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Audio\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Audio\">&gt; Audio</span></h2>\n<div class=\"noresize\">\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"text-align: center;\" data-expandtext=\"\u25bc\" data-collapsetext=\"\u25b2\">\n<caption style=\"white-space: nowrap;\">Audio\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Action</th>\n<th>Sound\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Spawning</td>\n<td><audio controls=\"\" preload=\"none\" width=\"320\" style=\"width:320px;max-width:100%;max-height:100%\" data-durationhint=\"15\" data-mwtitle=\"SnatcherRoarDistant.mp3\" data-mwprovider=\"local\"><source src=\"/images/SnatcherRoarDistant.mp3?af4605\" type=\"audio/mpeg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /><source src=\"/images/transcoded/SnatcherRoarDistant.mp3/SnatcherRoarDistant.mp3.ogg\" type=\"audio/ogg; codecs=&quot;vorbis&quot;\" data-transcodekey=\"ogg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /></audio>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Stepping</td>\n<td><audio controls=\"\" preload=\"none\" width=\"320\" style=\"width:320px;max-width:100%;max-height:100%\" data-durationhint=\"2\" data-mwtitle=\"SnatcherStep1.mp3\" data-mwprovider=\"local\"><source src=\"/images/SnatcherStep1.mp3?998a99\" type=\"audio/mpeg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /><source src=\"/images/transcoded/SnatcherStep1.mp3/SnatcherStep1.mp3.ogg\" type=\"audio/ogg; codecs=&quot;vorbis&quot;\" data-transcodekey=\"ogg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /></audio><br /